  ],
  "notes": "40 cells. Density is varied by GEOMETRY at a constant point count: ring width w in {0, 0.5, 1} and disk radius R in {0.25, 0.5}, so class balance never moves with density and the support never degenerates; w = 0 reproduces experiment 1's circle. Class balance is a THIRD axis, identical in both tasks, which is what makes the task-relevant and task-irrelevant grids comparable.\nFour measurement targets per cell where w > 0 (the ring and the circles at its inner edge, midline and outer edge), one where w = 0 since they coincide there. Each target carries its own A.1 nulls, registered into the instance because they are deterministic rigid motions fully described by the recipe.\nThe clearance between disk and ring is never below 0.5, and pairs of cells inside the grid share a clearance while differing in density -- (w=0.5, R=0.25) with (w=0, R=0.5) at 1.0, and (w=1, R=0.25) with (w=0.5, R=0.5) at 0.75 -- so the clearance is controlled without cells of its own. A matched-density pair falls out the same way: ring density 106.1 at (T=1000, n_ring=500, w=0.5) and at (T=5000, n_ring=1000, w=1.0).\nServer driver: notebooks/experiments/exp4_density_server.ipynb."
}